.627, 38.696, 38.766, 38.812, 38.859, 38.894, 38.963, 39.01, 39.08, 39.114, 39.161, 39.207, 39.23, 39.254, 39.335, 39.37, 39.416, 39.521, 39.718, 40.287, 40.333, 40.38, 40.403, 40.473, 40.542, 40.589, 40.612, 40.647, 40.682, 40.728, 40.775, 40.809, 40.856, 40.949, 41.03, 41.111, 41.193, 41.262, 41.309, 41.332, 41.355, 41.39, 41.425, 41.448, 41.518, 41.564, 41.657, 41.727, 41.773, 41.843, 41.924, 42.017, 42.179, 42.412, 42.609, 43.097, 43.143, 43.189, 43.236, 43.282, 43.329, 43.375, 43.422, 43.491, 43.561, 43.665, 43.747, 43.793, 43.863, 43.898, 43.921, 44.002, 44.037, 44.107, 44.176, 44.223, 44.292, 44.327, 44.35, 44.42, 44.455, 44.559, 44.606, 44.734, 44.815, 44.896, 44.966, 45.059, 45.186, 45.221, 45.291, 45.337, 45.372, 45.442, 45.488, 45.558, 45.639, 45.674, 45.72, 45.767, 45.802, 45.848, 45.883, 45.918, 45.999, 46.034, 46.231, 46.371, 46.568, 47.508]}, "text": "Now the stake goes into the eye. And here is something people rarely notice. Search the whole of Book Nine, and Homer never writes the words 'one eye'. He never mentions a forehead. He says 'the eye', and presumably his audience knew. For a plain statement, one eye in the forehead, we need a different poet. As for the blinding itself, Homer compares it to a shipwright boring a plank, and to a smith quenching an axe in water. That is all we need. The other Cyclopes hear the screaming and come to ask what is wrong. Pollifeemus shouts that Nobody is killing him. The others conclude that nobody is. They suggest he pray to Poseidon, and go back to bed.", "orig": "Now the stake goes into the eye. And here is something people rarely notice. Search the whole of Book Nine, and Homer never writes the words 'one eye'. He never mentions a forehead. He says 'the eye', and presumably his audience knew. For a plain statement, one eye in the forehead, we need a different poet. As for the blinding itself, Homer compares it to a shipwright boring a plank, and to a smith quenching an axe in water. That is all we need. The other Cyclopes hear the screaming and come to ask what is wrong. Polyphemus shouts that Nobody is killing him. The others conclude that nobody is. They suggest he pray to Poseidon, and go back to bed."}